# MASTER SOFTWARE ENGINEERING PROMPT
## Project: Monoprix Online — Premium E-commerce Supermarket Platform

### YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, software architect, UI/UX designer and quality assurance engineer.

Your responsibility is to design, architect, implement, test and deliver a complete, professional full-stack supermarket e-commerce application.

Do not approach this as a simple website-generation task.

Build a maintainable software product with real business workflows, reliable data handling, reusable components, clean architecture and a polished customer experience.

You must think like an engineer building software that a real supermarket could eventually operate.

---

# 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

Project name: Monoprix Online

Project type: Full-stack supermarket e-commerce platform.

Market: Sierra Leone.

Primary currency: SLE (Sierra Leonean Leone).

Primary audience:
- Supermarket customers.
- Supermarket administrators.
- Inventory and product management staff.
- Order processing staff.
- Delivery personnel.

Core objective:

Create a premium online supermarket where customers can browse products, search for groceries, add products to their shopping cart, check out, choose payment methods and arrange delivery.

The supermarket's staff must have an administrative dashboard for managing products, inventory, orders, payments and deliveries.

This is an independent concept demonstration. Do not claim that Monoprix has officially commissioned, approved or launched the application.

All sample business information, products, prices and transactions must be clearly identifiable as demonstration data.

